From d7ae98c6b0899c79d7a243f647cef552b1dd141a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:55:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] taskbar: null-check mControllers before reading
 cueBarController

The launcher dies at boot on this device and has to be restarted by hand:

    java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to read from field
        'com.android.launcher3.taskbar.CueBarController
         com.android.launcher3.taskbar.TaskbarControllers.cueBarController'
        on a null object reference
      at TaskbarNavButtonController.onRecentsButtonLayoutChanged(:289)
      at NavbarButtonsViewController.notifyRecentsButtonPosition(:588)
      at NavbarButtonsViewController.onBubbleBarLocationUpdated(:1403)
      at BubbleBarController.updateBubbleBarLocationInternal(:678)

The null object is mControllers, not cueBarController. mControllers is
assigned in init() and set back to null in onDestroy(), and the guard at
line 289 tests mControllers.cueBarController without first testing
mControllers -- so a bubble-bar location update delivered outside that
window dereferences null.

That reads as an oversight rather than an assumption: line 439 of this same
file already guards with "if (mControllers == null)". This adds the same
check to line 289.

It shows up on this device because desktop mode is enabled, which brings up
the taskbar and with it the bubble bar; the callback that triggers it does
not exist on a phone-shaped configuration.

Change-Id: I74ad475ef1ad3ac266454cac427f309760af4951
---
 .../android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarNavButtonController.java  | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarNavButtonController.java b/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarNavButtonController.java
index f2fd227df2..b0833787c7 100644
--- a/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarNavButtonController.java
+++ b/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarNavButtonController.java
@@ -286,7 +286,8 @@ public class TaskbarNavButtonController implements TaskbarControllers.LoggableTa
      */
     public void onRecentsButtonLayoutChanged(Rect bounds) {
         mSystemUiProxy.notifyRecentsButtonPositionChanged(bounds);
-        if (cueBarAceMigration() && mControllers.cueBarController != null) {
+        if (cueBarAceMigration() && mControllers != null
+                && mControllers.cueBarController != null) {
             mControllers.cueBarController.onRecentsButtonLayoutChanged(bounds);
         }
     }
-- 
